# NestJS + DDD Conventions

## Adding features

1. Business rules → domain entity methods (e.g. `conversation.canAddMessage()`)
2. Orchestration → `application/use-cases/<action>.use-case.ts`
3. Persistence → extend `I*Repository` in domain; implement in `infrastructure/repositories/`
4. HTTP → `presentation/*.controller.ts` with guards

## Repository mapping

```typescript
// Always map Prisma → domain explicitly
private toDomain(raw: PrismaRow): Entity { ... }
private toPersistence(entity: Entity): PrismaInput { ... }
```

## Guards (typical order)

`TenantGuard` → `JwtAuthGuard` → `PlanGuard` (when `@RequiresPlan` is set)

## Inject repository tokens

```typescript
@Inject(CONVERSATION_REPOSITORY)
private repo: IConversationRepository
```

## External services

- OpenAI → `infrastructure/services/openai.service.ts` (AI context only)
- Stripe → billing infrastructure only
- Never call OpenAI/Stripe from domain entities

## Streaming

Use SSE (`@Sse()`), not WebSockets, for AI token streams.
